  "hints": [
    "Construct the Binary-to-Excess-3 truth table for decimal inputs 0 through 9.",
    "Inputs 10 through 15 are invalid BCD inputs and may be treated as don't-care conditions.",
    "Use B, C and D as the select inputs of the 8×1 MUX.",
    "Use the 8×1 MUX to implement the W output bit.",
    "Connect I0 through I4 of the MUX to A and I5 through I7 to logic HIGH.",
    "Implement the remaining output bits X, Y and Z using basic gates.",
    "The Excess-3 output is WXYZ.",
    "Connect W, X, Y and Z to LED0, LED1, LED2 and LED3 respectively."
